ier this  evening at the u.n general assembly the  eu ambassador to the u.n um  condemned in the strongest form not only  russia but belarus's involvement in the  war i mean what is  how do you explain belarus's involvement  at this point  well initially as you know robert has  tried to  play a mediating role of course  under strong  pressure or direction from moscow  and that led to the so-called minsk  agreement that were supposed to  help solve the  ukraine crisis with the  the risk of separation from the two  eastern provinces now based on this uh  history  now that russia has  completely shifted its policy and led to  this  military occupation and invasion  parares has almost no choice but to take  part in this operation  and it had actually hosted a part of the  russian  troops that have invaded  ukraine from various territory and now  it's uh  still offering  it's it's its role  to host the  first  potential peace talks  but still  also hosting  russian missiles that have been  shot against ukraine from beerus  territory  and  on the issue of this referendum to allow  nuclear weapons to be stationed in  belarus the eu foreign policy chief has  weighed in and he said that this move is  is greatly worrying i mean how do you  expect the eu  to deal with this going forward  well i don't think that again um bearers  itself uh you know by by itself will  be subject of specific measures it's  it's part of uh  uh now reaction to the russian invasion  with the help of uh batteries bearers  and these subject  sanctions just like russia  it's it's already been actually  sanctioned because of uh  the uh  you know the result of the elections  that were considered  as um  uh  fraud or a coup by the the current  president  and so  and therefore  you know  the the focus really will be  on russia but  bearers will constantly  consequences for  for its action  uh in support of russia okay thank you  so much mark finneau for joining us from  geneva
 

